{"name":"Purple Blanket","hex":"#4a455d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"purple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour between red and blue; violet, though often closer to magenta.","Any non-spectral colour on the line of purples on a colour chromaticity diagram or a colour wheel between violet and red."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a purple hue.","Not predominantly red or blue, but having a mixture of Democrat and Republican support."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purple"},{"term":"blanket","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A heavy, loosely woven fabric, usually large and woollen, used for warmth while sleeping or resting.","A covering layer of anything."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["General; covering or encompassing everything."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blanket"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blanket","blocks":[{"text":"A blanket is a swath of smooth cloth large enough either to cover or to enfold most of the user's body and thick enough to keep the body warm by trapping radiant body heat that otherwise would be lost through convection and radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Lautrec_in_bed_1893.jpg/330px-Lautrec_in_bed_1893.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blanket","wikidata":"Q5852"},{"title":"Purple","blocks":[{"text":"Purple is a color similar in appearance to violet light. In the RYB color model historically used in the arts, purple is a secondary color created by combining red and blue pigments. In the CMYK color model used in modern printing, purple is made by combining magenta pigment with cyan pigment, black pigment, or both. In the RGB color model used in computer and television screens, purple is created by mixing red and blue light in order to create colors that appear similar to violet light. According to color theory, purple is considered a cool color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg/330px-Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purple","wikidata":"Q3257809"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Monet_dejeunersurlherbe.jpg/500px-Monet_dejeunersurlherbe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Monet_dejeunersurlherbe.jpg/500px-Monet_dejeunersurlherbe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Le déjeuner sur l'herbe, (right section) by Claude Monet","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMonet_dejeunersurlherbe.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/MARCHAND_DE_COUVERTURES_ET_SON_FOUGON.jpg/500px-MARCHAND_DE_COUVERTURES_ET_SON_FOUGON.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/MARCHAND_DE_COUVERTURES_ET_SON_FOUGON.jpg/1280px-MARCHAND_DE_COUVERTURES_ET_SON_FOUGON.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/MARCHAND_DE_COUVERTURES_ET_SON_FOUGON.jpg/500px-MARCHAND_DE_COUVERTURES_ET_SON_FOUGON.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Blanket vendors in a market in Algeria","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMARCHAND_DE_COUVERTURES_ET_SON_FOUGON.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Ghent_Altarpiece_D_-_Popes_-_Bishops.jpg/500px-Ghent_Altarpiece_D_-_Popes_-_Bishops.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/w